# Test automation: access-control coverage discipline

Ported from `.claude/agents/test-automation-engineer.md`. Section 9's Definition of Done requires
"access control is covered by tests per audience, per relationship path and per section, including
negative tests for every — cell." A feature is not done because it works for the happy path
someone demoed — it's done when the matrix is asserted, not just implemented.

## What to cover

- **Access-control test matrices.** For any section (S1–S16) or endpoint under test, build the
  cross-product that applies: audience (Self, Reporting line, Project line, PP, Colleague, Shared
  link, Full-profile-access holder) × relationship path (direct report, two-levels-up,
  department-manager, PM-of-project, DM-above-PM, assigned PP, no relationship) × section.
  **Reporting line and Project line are separate dimensions as of v1.5** — Project line loses
  S2/S3 and reduces S5 to CV+certificates, so don't collapse them into one "Manager line" case. HR
  Admin is config-only now, not an automatic full-access case; test Full-profile-access separately.
  Every `—` cell in `docs/access-control/section-matrix.md` needs a negative test asserting the API
  omits that section, not merely hides it.
- **Dual-gate tests (v1.5).** For access-role-scoped *and* permission-gated actions (approve/reject
  a candidate, close a request, edit the career timeline, record a departure), test all four
  quadrants of role×permission — only the both-present quadrant should succeed.
- **S7-specific negative tests.** An unflagged management note must be absent for both the
  employee and a PM in their respective read paths, and present for UM/DM/PP regardless of flags.
- **Colleague-whitelist tests.** Assert the colleague-view response contains *only* S1, S10
  (**dates only, no type as of v1.5**), and S11 project name — check the response shape, not just
  that a fixture lacks other fields. Separately test the campaign-author exception: name +
  completion status only, for that campaign's recipients, until it closes.
- **Shared-link tests (v1.5).** Link resolves only for its named, authenticated recipient; access
  re-checked per view (revoke the underlying relationship, confirm the link dies before expiry);
  never-share set enforced as {S3, S7, S13, S14} even if explicitly requested at creation.
- **Performance tests** for All Employees: 500+ records, arbitrary filters, derived fields,
  permission resolution included — must respond within 2 seconds (spec Section 7).
- **Integration resilience tests** for timetracker/PeopleForce: simulate timeouts, 5xx, malformed
  payloads; assert graceful degradation rather than a broken request or a silent
  grant/deny-on-failed-lookup.
- **Follow the agreed test architecture** if a testing-architecture ADR exists in
  `docs/decisions/` — test pyramid shape, fixture strategy, unit/integration/e2e split — rather
  than an ad hoc pattern per service.

## Test data discipline

Fixtures for a 500+ person org must be pseudonymised per the `pseudonymized-data-only` rule — real
structure and volume, fabricated identities. No exemption for test data.

## You verify, you don't set policy

Whether a matrix cell should be R, RW, or `—` is a spec/product question — see
`docs/access-control/section-matrix.md` and spec Sections 2–3. If a test reveals the matrix and
the implementation disagree, flag it rather than silently adjusting the test to match whichever
side is more convenient.
